.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-deliveries - Webhook deliveries across accounts: what a merchant was told, and whether it landed


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin deliveries [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List webhook delivery attempts across every account, newest first, each with the
subscription it went to and that subscription's account.

.PP
Start from what is at hand: --payment (what was this payment's merchant told), --webhook
(what is this subscription failing on), or neither with --status failed for everything
that is not landing. --response-code tells a receiver's crashes (500) from its refusals
(401, 429). The gateway keeps 15 days of attempts.

.PP
The event body (payload) is left out: it is the whole event, several kilobytes a row.
--payload includes it.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for deliveries

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--payload\fP[=false]
	Include each delivery's event body

.PP
\fB--payment\fP=""
	Only deliveries for this payment: its id (UUID) or its rail0_id (0x…)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--response-code\fP=""
	Only deliveries the receiver answered with exactly this HTTP status

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	Only deliveries at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort by created_at or status (prefix - for descending; default: newest first)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=""
	Only deliveries that were delivered or failed

.PP
\fB--topic\fP=""
	Only deliveries of this event topic

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	Only deliveries at/before this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--webhook\fP=""
	Only this subscription's deliveries (webhook id)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin deliveries --status failed --since 2026-11-26T00:00:00Z
  rail0 admin deliveries --payment 0xrail0Id…
  rail0 admin deliveries --webhook 01a0f3c2-… --status failed --response-code 500
  rail0 admin deliveries --topic payments.captured --pretty
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP
